               <exData contentType="text/html">
                  <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p style="font-size:11pt;font-weight:bold;text-decoration:underline;letter-spacing:0in">Approved for Probationary or Academic Plan:</p><p style="font-size:9pt;text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in">If approved, your appeal will be granted for either: (1)<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span><span style="font-weight:bold">one</span> Probationary semester or (2) an Academic Plan spanning multiple semesters, depending on your specific circumstances. We will continue to monitor your SAP after each semester to determine if you are eligible for financial aid for the subsequent term(s). If your appeal was granted Probationary, you must make SAP after your approved term or your SAP status will again be suspended. If approved for an Academic Plan, you must meet the conditions of your plan each term or your SAP status will again be suspended. If SAP suspended, you are not eligible for financial aid.</p><p style="font-size:9pt;text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p></body>
               </exData>
            </value>
            <font typeface="Calibri" baselineShift="0pt"/>
